          {
            "id": "79",
            "title": "Religious Education & Formation",
            "alias": "religious-education-formation",
            "categoryId": "277",
            "categoryTitle": "",
            "introtext": "\t<p>The Gospel tells us that we are called to know the Truth and that \"the Truth will set us free!\"  At St. Mary we strive to be a beacon of that truth for all ages.</p>\n<p><strong>St. Mary Catholic School</strong> strives to educate our children in the Gospel by incorporating it into all aspects of their daily life.</p>\n<p>For those who do not attend St. Mary Catholic School, the Religious Education Program at St. Mary's serves children grades preschool-12.</p>\n<p>For all middle school - high school students, St. Mary strives to offer youth ministry opportunities throughout the year.</p>\n<p>Perhaps you are an adult and are not Catholic.  If you would like to learn more about the Catholic Church, even if you are not yet ready to become Catholic, then we offer a variety of opportunities.  See our <a href=\"index.php?option=com_content&amp;view=article&amp;id=15&amp;catid=21&amp;Itemid=127\">R.C.I.A. (Rite of Christian Initiation for Adults)</a> page for more information.</p>\n<p>Ongoing adult education opportunities are an essential part of every Catholic's journey.  St. Mary offers a variety or educational Bible studies, teachings, adult classes, and more.</p>\n<p>Perhaps you are gifted with a deep and rich understanding of the Catholic faith and would like to share that faith with others.  Please contact us and let us know how you would like to get involved.</p>",
            "fulltext": "",
            "state": "-2",
            "access": "1"
          }
        ]
      },
